# Frontend has no separate .env source — see ../../.env.example (single source, ${VAR} interpolation).
# Backend validation rules for these keys: ../../docs/env-validation.md
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL must be a URL when set; NEXT_PUBLIC_PORT a numeric port).
# Copy root .env.example to ../../.env for local overrides (never commit .env/secrets).
# Precedence: shell process.env > root .env file > built-in defaults (pm2 injects into process.env;
# Next.js inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_* into the browser bundle at `next build` time,
# from process.env at dev time or from .env.local only for service-local overrides).
#
# Resolved keys consumed by apps/frontend (all optional, defaults shown):
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=${APP_BACKEND_SOCKET} (dev default http://localhost:3000)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PORT=3001 (dev: `next dev` port; prod standalone serves :3000, host-mapped to 8080)
# Only create apps/frontend/.env.local for service-local overrides (e.g. remote API URL);
# prefer setting values in the root .env so compose + pm2 stay in sync.
